loop 14 | Tool=Write, Args={"file_path":"/home/silimon/.claude/projects/-home-silimon-MCP-Auto/memory/mcp-paperswithcode-setup.md","content":"---\nname: mcp-paperswithcode setup\ndescription: How hbg/mcp-paperswithcode MCP server is installed and configured\ntype: reference\n---\n\nRule: The `hbg/mcp-paperswithcode` MCP server (GitHub repo ID 949611900) is installed at `/home/silimon/MCP-Auto/mcp_server/949611900_hbg_mcp-paperswithcode/` with its own dedicated venv at `.venv`.\n\n**Why:** This MCP server provides 20 tools for searching and reading research papers from the PapersWithCode API, plus author, conference, and research area lookups. It was set up as part of the MCP-Auto project to give AI assistants access to academic paper data.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- **Start command:** `/home/silimon/MCP-Auto/mcp_server/949611900_hbg_mcp-paperswithcode/.venv/bin/python -m mcp_paperswithcode.server`\n- **Type:** stdio\n- **CWD:** `/home/silimon/MCP-Auto/mcp_server/949611900_hbg_mcp-paperswithcode`\n- **Config file:** Project `.claude/settings.json` (or `~/.claude/settings.json`) under the key `949611900_hbg_mcp-paperswithcode`\n- **No API keys or env vars required** — uses the public PapersWithCode API at `https://paperswithcode.com/api/v1`\n- If reinstalling: clone the repo, run `uv venv .venv && uv pip install -e .` inside the cloned directory, then add the stdio config.\n"}
